    "summary": "Task t9 adds the section \"How a request's size is measured\" to docs/daemon.md and corrects every page, prompt and comment found to say that a size is classified, picked by a model or defaulted to M. The gate failed the Task twice on that check: first for four places (fixed in 3ae59391 with the others a wider search found), then for one sentence in design/analyze-plan-builder.md (fixed in cbbe5e3e with two example lines on the same page). src/shared/classify.ts was left: it is an unused generic classifier type with its own scale, not the analyzer's. The five suites were compared by test name with the Story's baseline (no test that passed before fails after; four names gone, each named), and four were rerun unchanged after the wording fixes. Origin was merged with --no-ff, pushed, and the daemon updated, each on the stakeholder's word. The live check ran two requests through the daemon: the same code request measured S on one directory and XL on the whole repository, each with its counts and the stated M as the hint, with no size-picking call. The installed daemon is at 67b5ca52 and does not have the wording fixes, which change no behaviour. The repository run also showed a defect that is not this Story's (a child plan's task outputs share files with its parent's), recorded in the live record and not yet filed.",
